                            <comment id="15896747" author="ess_ess" created="Mon, 6 Mar 2017 05:00:11 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I looked into this issue&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;While I was checking this issue(I used sample bank data from &apos;Zeppelin Tutorial/Basic Features (Spark)&apos; and  my query was &apos;%sql select * from bank&apos;), Three things crossed my path&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;1* Multiple groups in chart doesn&apos;t work for stacked-bar charts&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;2* Grouping in  pie charts to be a bit un-intuitive. I&apos;m not sure if that is a bug.&lt;br/&gt;
I set&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;key: &apos;marital&apos;
values: &apos;avg(balance)&apos;
groups: &apos;job&apos;
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;still there were no visible grouping in the pie chart. It should group sectors as &apos;single.primary, single.secondary&apos;, right? &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;3* Grouping in bar charts work with &apos;grouped bar chart&apos;. But the derived data feels buggy in the same paragraph. When I tried this setting-&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;key: &apos;marital&apos;
value: &apos;avg(balance)&apos;
groupby: (&apos;job&apos; + &apos;education&apos;)
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;the y-value in graph for &apos;primary.housemaid.balance&apos; on marital=single is 26,965. When I cross checked, there were three results:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&apos;table-wrap&apos;&gt;
&lt;table class=&apos;confluenceTable&apos;&gt;&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th class=&apos;confluenceTh&apos;&gt;age&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;td class=&apos;confluenceTd&apos;&gt;job&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&apos;confluenceTd&apos;&gt;marital&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&apos;confluenceTd&apos;&gt;education&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&apos;confluenceTd&apos;&gt;balance&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&apos;confluenceTd&apos;&gt;31&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&apos;confluenceTd&apos;&gt;housemaid&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&apos;confluenceTd&apos;&gt;single&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&apos;confluenceTd&apos;&gt;primary&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&apos;confluenceTd&apos;&gt;26965&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&apos;confluenceTd&apos;&gt;39&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&apos;confluenceTd&apos;&gt;housemaid&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&apos;confluenceTd&apos;&gt;single&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&apos;confluenceTd&apos;&gt;primary&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&apos;confluenceTd&apos;&gt;109&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&apos;confluenceTd&apos;&gt;42&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&apos;confluenceTd&apos;&gt;housemaid&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&apos;confluenceTd&apos;&gt;single&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&apos;confluenceTd&apos;&gt;primary&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&apos;confluenceTd&apos;&gt;5774&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The average would be somewhere around 10000. Is this expected?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
